{"files":[{"content":"#include <limits.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nstatic char *bucket_sort(char *records, int record_width, long int size,\n                         int offset, int nbuckets) {\n    char *buffer;\n    char *source = records;\n    char *destination;\n    size_t counts[256];\n    size_t positions[256];\n    size_t width;\n\n    (void)offset;\n    (void)nbuckets;\n\n    if (size <= 1 || record_width <= 1)\n        return records;\n\n    width = (size_t)record_width;\n    if ((size_t)size > (size_t)-1 / width) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"Sort buffer size is too large\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    buffer = (char *)malloc((size_t)size * width);\n    if (buffer == NULL) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"Unable to allocate sort buffer\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n    destination = buffer;\n\n    for (int position = record_width - 2; position >= 0; --position) {\n        size_t next = 0;\n\n        memset(counts, 0, sizeof(counts));\n        for (long int i = 0; i < size; ++i) {\n            size_t source_offset = (size_t)i * width;\n            unsigned char key = (unsigned char)source[source_offset + (size_t)position];\n            ++counts[key];\n        }\n\n        for (int key = 0; key < 256; ++key) {\n            positions[key] = next;\n            next += counts[key];\n        }\n\n        for (long int i = 0; i < size; ++i) {\n            size_t source_offset = (size_t)i * width;\n            unsigned char key = (unsigned char)source[source_offset + (size_t)position];\n            size_t destination_offset = positions[key]++ * width;\n            memcpy(destination + destination_offset, source + source_offset, width);\n        }\n\n        char *temporary = source;\n        source = destination;\n        destination = temporary;\n    }\n\n    if (source == records)\n        free(buffer);\n    else\n        free(records);\n\n    return source;\n}\n\nstatic void load(char **strings_out, long int *count_out, int *width_out,\n                 int *offset_out, int *buckets_out) {\n    int payload_length;\n    int offset;\n    int bucket_count;\n    long int count;\n    char *strings;\n    size_t width;\n\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &payload_length) != 1) {\n        printf(\"ERROR len\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%ld\", &count) != 1) {\n        printf(\"ERROR n\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &offset) != 1) {\n        printf(\"ERROR offset\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &bucket_count) != 1) {\n        printf(\"ERROR nbucket\\n\");\n        exit(1);\n    }\n\n    if (payload_length < 0 || payload_length == INT_MAX || count < 0 ||\n        (count > 0 && payload_length == 0)) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"Invalid input dimensions\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    width = (size_t)payload_length + 1;\n    if ((size_t)count > (size_t)-1 / width) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"Input size is too large\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    strings = (char *)calloc((size_t)count, width);\n    if (strings == NULL && count > 0) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"Unable to allocate input strings\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    for (long int i = 0; i < count; ++i) {\n        if (fscanf(stdin, \"%s\", strings + (size_t)i * width) != 1) {\n            printf(\"ERROR %ld\\n\", i);\n            exit(1);\n        }\n    }\n\n    *strings_out = strings;\n    *count_out = count;\n    *width_out = (int)width;\n    *offset_out = offset;\n    *buckets_out = bucket_count;\n}\n\nstatic void save(const char *strings, long int count, int width) {\n    for (long int i = 0; i < count; ++i)\n        printf(\"%s\\n\", strings + (size_t)i * (size_t)width);\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    char *strings = NULL;\n    long int count = 0;\n    int width = 0;\n    int offset;\n    int buckets;\n\n    load(&strings, &count, &width, &offset, &buckets);\n    strings = bucket_sort(strings, width, count, offset, buckets);\n    save(strings, count, width);\n    free(strings);\n\n    return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n","path":"src/bucketsort.c"}],"hypothesis":"Stable LSD counting passes over each record’s bytes should replace potentially quadratic per-bucket insertion sorting while preserving strcmp ordering, including variable-length strings through zero-padded records.","notes":"Retains the measured, correctness-checked LSD counting-pass idea and applies it to the complete program. Input and output formats remain unchanged; the controller should validate and time the integrated result.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":["a981acbf59e44c56"],"transformations":["Replace per-bucket insertion sorting of indices with stable least-significant-digit counting passes over all string bytes.","Reuse one scratch buffer and scatter full records into contiguous ranges on each pass; zero-initialize input records to preserve ordering of variable-length strings."]}